FILED s531c (Opus agent, 2026-11-01), from #4083's non-keyword-position probes.  PRE-EXISTING (base ade297e7 identical).  LOUD (a drop).  Rare in real code (no board / everyday row known).

    sub unless { "U(@_)" }  sub while { "W(@_)" }
    print &unless(5), " ", &while(6, 7), "\n";
    print main::unless(8), "\n";
  perl 5.40.3: U(5) W(6 7) / U(8)
  PCL: PCL: statement dropped ... line 2: print &unless(5), ... -- statement keyword `unless` used as a function   (the qualified `main::unless(8)` works)
Probe: scratch/s531c/p/amp.pl in the s531c worktree.

PPI reads `&unless` as ONE Symbol (correct).  The refusal is Pl/ExprToCL.pm gen_funcall_form's #374 guard (`statement_keywords->{ $fn->content }` -> die), reached with a Word `unless` -- so the `&NAME` Symbol is turned into a plain funcall Word somewhere upstream (PExpr's `&NAME(LIST)` path, #3859's p-amp-spread neighbourhood) and the guard cannot tell it came from an `&`.  Fix shape: the `&`-call keeps its origin to the guard (or the guard asks the node's form), so only a BARE keyword reaching the funcall generator is refused.


